  "time_scale_note": "Contacts are given in UT computed by GSFC with its predicted Delta T. Each eclipse's exact Delta T is taken from its own greatest-eclipse line (TD and UT, both to 0.1 s) and every contact is converted back to TD = UT + Delta T, which is what the comparison uses. Using today's leap-second UTC instead would misplace the contacts by about 6 s.",
